ake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-386.json" "file_sha256" "3c42be9dd29c6e8f2123ecdfeb13fcf9e6ea015ab84867a3e4d1f4830c24014d"} {"question" "e-387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-387.json" "file_sha256" "7cec0181184a46f59e74b7f950dd156470d2bf15446eefc33a9cf836905ad2e7"} {"question" "e-387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-387.json" "file_sha256" "7cec0181184a46f59e74b7f950dd156470d2bf15446eefc33a9cf836905ad2e7"} {"question" "e-3890" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f'(x) = \\dfrac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} - 2x,$ then $f(x)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-3890.json" "file_sha256" "a17abf396bbc6081c69beb80f9f499937dad5a2d7a89b0e215cac2f6a83eef6a"} {"question" "e-3890" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm dx = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-3890.json" "file_sha256" "a17abf396bbc6081c69beb80f9f499937dad5a2d7a89b0e215cac2f6a83eef6a"} {"question" "e-388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {x^2+2}{x^2 + 1}\\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-388.json" "file_sha256" "aeb64e9317290a763a63c2b0cb595da2cf609f3213d2772d2fe136a995bab5fb"} {"question" "e-388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1+1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1} \\textrm dx = \\arctan(x),\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987603/example-388.json" "file_sha256" "aeb64e9317290a763a63c2b0cb595da2cf609f3213d2772d2fe136a995bab5fb"} {"question" "q-19100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)+C"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-cap