 function name and argument; these corrections restore those boundaries. The Incorrect grade concerns submitted arccsc, not the reviewed answer."}] "usage" {"q-19100" [] "e-386" [] "q-19090" [] "e-387" [] "e-3890" [] "q-19102" [] "e-388" []} "basis" 1085 "retractions" [[17592186064454 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}dx$?"] [17592186064455 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{11}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx$?"] [17592186064455 :question/answer-fields 17592186061379] [17592186064456 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{3x^{2}}{x^{2} + 1}dx$?"] [17592186064456 :question/answer-fields 17592186061385] [17592186063973 :question/problem "Calculate the indefinite integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186063973 :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x = \\arcsin (x) + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}dx &= 3\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}dx \\\\\n&= 3\\arcsin (x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063974 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186063974 :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{2}{1 + x^{2}}dx &= 2\\int\\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= 2\\arctan x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063976 :question/problem "If $f'(x) = \\dfrac{5}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} - 2x$, then $f(x)=$"] [17592186063976 :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm dx = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, x\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= \\intf^{′}(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\frac{5}{\\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}} - 2x)dx \\\\ = \\int\\frac{5}{\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx - \\int2xdx \\\\ = 5\\int\\frac{1}{\\mid x\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}dx - 2\\intxdx \\\\\n&= 5arcsec(x) - 2 \\cdot \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C \\\\\n&= 5arcsec(x) - x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186063975 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {x^2+2}{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186063975 :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2} + 2}{x^{2} + 1} &= \\frac{x^{2} + 1 + 1}{x^{2} + 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x^{2} + 1} + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1} \\textrm dx = \\arctan(x)\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{x^{2} + 2}{x^{2} + 1}dx &= \\int(1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1})dx \\\\\n&= \\int1dx + \\int\\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}dx \\\\\n&= x + \\arctan (x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061374 17592186061375 17592186061376 17592186061377 17592186061378 17592186061380 17592186061381 17592186061382 17592186061383 17592186061384 17592186061386 17592186061387 17592186061388 17592186061389 17592186061390] "immutable_fields" [[17592186061373 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061373 :answer-field/id] [17592186061373 :answer-field/key] [17592186061373 :answer-field/type] [17592186061379 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061379 :answer-field/id] [17592186061379 :answer-field/key] [17592186061379 :answer-field/type] [17592186061385 :answer-field/correct] [17592186061385 :answer-field/id] [17592186061385 :answer-field/key] [17592186061385 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
